n hand, I have B1, B2, B2, B3, B3. So I have at least one of each number. So I can group them as a chow: B1, B2, B3. That would be a concealed chow if I keep them together. But currently my hand is not organized into melds; melds are only exposed ones. So I could have a concealed chow in hand. So actually I may already have three melds: two exposed chows and one concealed chow (B1,B2,B3). Then I need one more meld and a pair. So currently: Melds: [W3,W4,W5], [T1,T2,T3], and concealed chow [B1,B2,B3]. That's three melds. Then leftover tiles: B2, B3, B5, F1, F1. So I have B2, B3, B5, F1, F1. I need one more meld and a pair. Possible: pair F1, and meld from B2,B3,B5? Could form another chow B3,B4,B5 if I get B4, or B2,B3,B4 if I get B4. Or pung of B2 or B3 if I get a third. Or pung of F1 if I get third F1. So I am close to winning.  \n\nNow, which tile to discard? I have 8 hand tiles after considering concealed chow: Actually total hand tiles are 8, but if I consider B1,B2,B3 as a chow, that uses 3 tiles, leaving 5 tiles: B2, B3, B5, F1, F1. So I need to discard one. Options:  \n- Discard B5: keeps B2,B3 pair potential and F1 pair. B5 is isolated.  \n- Discard B2: keeps B3,B5,F1,F1. Then pair could be F1, and need meld from B3,B5? Not good.  \n- Discard B3: similar.  \n- Discard F1: keeps Bamboo tiles, but loses valuable wind pung chance.  \nSo best is discard B5, as it is least useful for forming melds or pair. B5 only connects with B4,B6 or B3,B4 or B5,B6,B7. I have no B4 or B6. Unshown B4:4, B6:3, so possible but less likely than making pung of B2 or B3 or F1. Also, keeping F1 gives high point potential.  \n\nAlso consider tile safety: history shows opponents have discarded some tiles. Next player history: played T2, W4, T9, W7, W8, T1, W3. No Bamboo except T tiles. Across player: played J3, T4, F3, Peng W7, T9, B9, T6, T1, B7. They discarded B9 and B7, so maybe safe to discard B5? Previous player: played W4, W4, W8, Chi T8, T3, B5, B1, B8, F2. They discarded B5 and